-- title:
--   q-LU factorization of the Gaussian Toeplitz matrix
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $x, z \in K$ with $z \ne 0$, $q = x^2$, and $n \in \mathbb N$ with $(q;q)_i \ne 0$ for all $i < n$. Let $T = $ `gaussToep x z n` be the $n \times n$ Gaussian Toeplitz matrix with entries $x^{(i-j)^2} z^{i-j}$, let $\Gamma = $ `Gam q n` be the diagonal matrix of the q-Pochhammer weights and $L(c)$, $U(c)$ the lower/upper triangular Toeplitz matrices of a sequence $c$. With $b^{+}_h = x^{h^2} z^h/(q;q)_h$ and $b^{-}_h = x^{h^2} z^{-h}/(q;q)_h$,
--
--   $$T = \Gamma\, L(b^{-})\, \Gamma^{-1}\, U(b^{+})\, \Gamma.$$
--
--   This explicit LU decomposition is the algebraic core of the segmented Gaussian inverse in the round-six stack.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6QLU.qLU (x z : K) (n : ℕ) (hz : z ≠ 0) (hq : ∀ i < n, qpoch (x ^ 2) i ≠ 0) :
--       gaussToep x z n =
--         Gam (x ^ 2) n * lowT (bP x z⁻¹) * GamInv (x ^ 2) n * upT (bP x z) * Gam (x ^ 2) n
--   ```
